-- tests-independent.l4: independent test author (review run dst-rev-coa2). One #ASSERT per scenario of ANSWERS.md, expected values written BEFORE any module was opened.
-- Each comment: scenario number | provision and text line number (of inputs/ukpga-2006-46.txt) | the sentence or ruling of the Commons guide relied on (Guide: ...).
-- CBC = one of the six case-by-case questions: an encoding that answers differently is AMBIGUOUS, not ENCODER. Answers: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING (the encoding's own convention).
-- Scenarios asked through the seat layer (the *-seat.l4 questions) are the ones whose comment starts with SEAT (602-642). Layer-1 rules are called only where noted (561, 580).
-- A number with a letter (28a, 28b) is one scenario with two answers. GAP lines at the end list the scenarios of ANSWERS.md that the encoding has no function for.

